From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: ave: take P010 before the coded format
 is set

FFmpeg's hevc_v4l2m2m sets the raw (OUTPUT) format before the coded
(CAPTURE) one. The driver accepted P010 only when the coded format was
already HEVC, so while CAPTURE still had its H.264 default it changed the
request to NV12, and FFmpeg gave up ("Encoder requires nv12 pixel
format"); HEVC Main 10 could not be encoded with stock FFmpeg on the M4.
FFmpeg also never sets the HEVC profile control, so a P010 session would
then have been refused as Main with 16-bit input.

Take P010 on OUTPUT whatever the coded format is, turn it back into NV12
when the coded format is set to H.264, and let P010 input select Main 10
for HEVC. An explicit Main 10 request with NV12 input is still refused.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-sess.c |  9 ++++++---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-sess.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-sess.c
index e47337b611..74c02a4645 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-sess.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-sess.c
@@ -174,11 +174,14 @@ static int ave_sess_params(struct ave_ctx *ctx, struct ave_params *p)
 	/*
 	 * HEVC Main 10 encodes P010 input; Main encodes NV12. The firmware
 	 * takes 16-bit samples for Main 10 (macOS converts 8-bit input to that
-	 * first), so other pairings are refused rather than converted.
+	 * first), so other pairings are refused rather than converted. P010
+	 * input selects Main 10 by itself: the profile control defaults to
+	 * Main, and clients that never set it (FFmpeg's hevc_v4l2m2m) would
+	 * otherwise be refused.
 	 */
 	if ((p->codec == AVE_CODEC_HEVC &&
-	     ctx->hevc_profile == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE_MAIN_10) !=
-	    (p->sample_bytes == 2))
+	     (ctx->hevc_profile == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE_MAIN_10 ||
+	      p->sample_bytes == 2)) != (p->sample_bytes == 2))
 		return -EINVAL;
 	if (p->sample_bytes == 2) {
 		/* Only the 9003 layout's Main 10 fields are mapped. */
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
index d46a810e24..ced9d9bbd6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
@@ -92,13 +92,15 @@ static void ave_clamp_size(u32 coded, u32 *w, u32 *h)
  * Raw NV12 or P010, one buffer: Y plane, then interleaved CbCr at half
  * height. P010 holds 10-bit samples in the high bits of 16-bit words; it
  * is the input for HEVC Main 10. @coded is the context's coded format,
- * which limits the size.
+ * which limits the size. P010 is taken whatever the coded format is at
+ * this point, since clients such as FFmpeg set the raw side first; a later
+ * switch of the coded side to H.264 turns it back into NV12.
  */
 static void ave_fill_raw(struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *f, u32 coded)
 {
 	u32 stride, height, bytes;
 
-	if (f->pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010 || coded != V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC)
+	if (f->pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010)
 		f->pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12;
 	bytes = f->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010 ? 2 : 1;
 	ave_clamp_size(coded, &f->width, &f->height);
@@ -245,6 +247,12 @@ static int ave_s_fmt_cap(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 	pix->ycbcr_enc = ctx->src_fmt.ycbcr_enc;
 	pix->quantization = ctx->src_fmt.quantization;
 	ctx->dst_fmt = *pix;
+	/* H.264 takes 8-bit input only. */
+	if (pix->pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC &&
+	    ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010) {
+		ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12;
+		ave_fill_raw(&ctx->src_fmt, pix->pixelformat);
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
